<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49836" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūnĭ-formis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		unus-forma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having only one shape</i> or <i>form</i>, <i>uniform</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simplex quiddam et uniforme doceri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facies deorum dearumque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 259, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humanum genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Asclep. p. 98, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alimonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">institutum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Epit. 9</span></i>
			
			<i>med.—Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūnĭformĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>in one and the same manner</i>, <i>uniformly</i>, <i><span class="en">App. Asclep. p. 77,
			18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 88</span></i>.</div>
